      "writtenOn": "2015-04-28T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand. Why doesn\u0027t it work to do \n\n\n\n  tup :\u003d optionsTuple{}\n  if err :\u003d Unmarshal(\u0026tup); .. {\n\n  }\n  \n  valStr :\u003d \"\"\n  if len(tup.Val) \u003e 0 {\n     val :\u003d optTupVal{}\n     if err :\u003d Unmarshal(\u0026val) .. { }\n     valStr \u003d string(val.Val)\n  }\n\nif the length prefixes are off, Unmarshal would detect that, no?",
      "revId": "c56e67bd9af6529330b21cf329a52208d65bc63e",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
