    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "500f6eb1_733cd242",
        "filename": "ssh/certs.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 6190
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-04-28T18:08:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You cannot do: \nif err :\u003d Unmarshal(\u0026tup); \nsince you need to give to Unmarshal a slice - that is, indicate where the piece that you want to Unmarshal ends.\n\nTake a look at the latest patch set (#8), I used Unmarshal but I have to do the following:\n  keylen :\u003d binary.BigEndian.Uint32(in)\n  vallen :\u003d binary.BigEndian.Uint32(in[keylen+4:])\nand then use those values to tell Unmarshal what to parse and where the limits are.\n\nDo you like it?  It would be nice if there were a length offset for the whole key/value pair at the beginning...  I wonder if using parseString - with its nice return of \"rest\" - would be a more natural, less magical, easier to understand and less error prone way to parse this than Unmarshal...  Let me know what you think!",
      "parentUuid": "f00b02a7_709a86ed",
      "revId": "c56e67bd9af6529330b21cf329a52208d65bc63e",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
